{ seats } seats · ${ seatCost }/mo
:::
::: div .summary-line
Add-ons · ${ addons }/mo
:::
:::

::: div .annual-block
Billed annually: **${ annualBill }/yr** — you save **${ annualSaved }** vs. monthly.
:::

::: div .summary-cta
:button "Reset everything" -> base reset; seats reset; analytics reset; sso reset; priority reset
:::

A month-to-month list price would run **${ annual }/yr**. Choose yearly at checkout to lock the discount.
:::
:::

:::

## 4 · Start your trial

Drop in your details and we'll spin up your **${ total }/mo** workspace — no charge for 14 days.

::: div .checkout-card
:form action="/__wd/echo" into receipt
:input name placeholder="Your name"
:input email placeholder="Work email"
:submit "Start 14-day trial"
:endform

:if receipt
::: div .receipt
### You're in 🎉

We've reserved your plan at **${ total }/mo** ({ seats } seats). Confirmation sent at **{ receipt.at }** — check your inbox to finish setup.
:::
:else
::: div .checkout-note
Your plan today: **${ total }/mo** · billed annually at **${ annualBill }/yr**. You can change tiers or seats any time.
:::
:endif

:if receipt_error
::: div .checkout-error
Something went wrong: { receipt_error }
:::
:endif
:::

---

## It's just Markdown

No JSX, no `useState`, no pricing library. The tier buttons, the seat stepper, the feature toggles, the live total, the upsell hints, and the checkout are all directives in one `.wd` file. The pricing engine is a single `:computed` line:

<details class="source-reveal"><summary>View source — it's Markdown</summary>

```wd
:state base = 20
:state seats = 3
:state analytics = false
:state sso = false
:state priority = false

:computed total = base + seats*8 + analytics*25 + sso*50 + priority*40
:computed annualBill = total*10
:computed annualSaved = total*2

The price is ${ total }/mo.

::: card .tier .on when base == 20
:button "Select Team" -> base = 20
:::

:button "–" -> seats -= 1
:button "+" -> seats++

::: card .feature .on when analytics
:if analytics
:button "Remove" -> analytics toggle
:else
:button "Add analytics" -> analytics toggle
:endif
:::

:if sso and not priority
Teams that turn on SSO almost always add Priority support.
:endif

:if total > 150
You've unlocked the annual discount.
:endif

:button "Reset everything" -> base reset; seats reset; analytics reset; sso reset; priority reset
```

</details>

Booleans coerce in arithmetic, so `analytics*25` is `25` when the toggle is on and `0` when it's off — that one rule is the whole pricing engine. [Read the docs](/docs/) or [see the reactive page](/reactive/).

:::

</main>

